<title>REPUBLIC OF IRELAND: Irish hauliers end port blockades pending talks.</title>
<headline>Irish hauliers end port blockades pending talks.</headline>
<dateline>DUBLIN 1997-06-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish hauliers who were blockading two Irish ports in a pay dispute with shipping companies agreed on Friday to lift their blockade pending talks with the shipping firms and Irish transport minister Alan Dukes.</p>
<p>The hauliers had been blocking traffic in Dublin docks since earlier this week and extended the protest to Rosslare, on the southwest coast, on Friday morning.</p>
<p>They later agreed to end the blockade but warned it would be reimposed if the talks did not lead to negotiations for new pay rates.</p>
<p>The hauliers are demanding a 50-percent increase in haulage rates which they say have stood still or even declined for 15 years.</p>
<p>-- Dublin Newsroom +353 1 676 9779</p>
</text>
